  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.13 - FIX (CUDA, since 5.8.11; upgrade from 5.8.11 / 5.8.12): prompts over 512 tokens on models whose attention v projection has a different block type than q / k (common in Q4_K_M files: llama3, qwen2.5) could get badly wrong logits (up to 27 off, measured), because the v projection running on a second CUDA stream shared prefill scratch memory with the q / k projection. Fixed; overlap on and off are bit-identical. (Workaround for 5.8.11 / 5.8.12: env GGUF_OVERLAP_V=0.) Also: the opt-in int8 activations (GGUF_INT8_ACT=1, off by default) now cover prefill too, on int8 tensor cores (Ollama's MMQ scheme): qwen3:1.7b Q4_K_M prefill +9% at 1,830 tokens, +22% at 29 on an RTX 4070. See CHANGELOG.md.",
